e,"_score_int_coverage":3.7,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":3.083377717902124,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":false,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":20.4,"_gate_accruals":-0.06841916497666559,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":56.9,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.15101599063492457,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":71.1,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.1006503411482248,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":6,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":66.7,"_gate_spread":-0.08351120884887374,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":12.920593440699362,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.032588960000048475,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":44.2,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0765639994281562,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":96.2,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.02104178810955437,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":76.3,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.048274175718746766,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":19.5,"_gate_insider_own":0.05192,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":34.6,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"EverCommerce Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides integrated software-as-a-service solutions for service-based small and medium-sized businesses in the United States and internationally. Its solutions include business management software that offers route-based dispatching and medical practice management solutions; billing and payment solutions comprising e-invoicing, mobile payments, and integrated payment processing; customer experience solutions, which include reputation management and messaging solutions; and marketing technology solutions that cover websites, hosting, and digital lead generation. The company also provides EverPro suite of solutions for home services; EverHealth suite of solutions for health services; and EverWell suite of solutions for wellness services. In addition, the company offers professional services, such as consulting, implementation, and training; and sells hardware products. It serves home service professionals, such as home improvement contractors and home maintenance technicians; physician practices and therapists in the health services industry; and salon owners within the wellness sector. The company was formerly known as PaySimple Holdings, Inc. and changed its name to EverCommerce Inc. in December 2020. EverCommerce Inc. was incorporated in 2016 and is headquartered in Denver, Colorado.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Alexander  Goor | CEO & Director | Age 53","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $327K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers. Each employee generates $61K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $16K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["EverCommerce Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $1.1B market cap on $589M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding. Operating margins are expanding by +3.9pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 0% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $109M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 19 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 6.33\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 1.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 7.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 5.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Goodwill represents 65% of total assets \u2014 a large impairment risk hanging over book value","sev":"red","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.07555073018248501},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $3.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 65/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"EverCommerce (EVCM), What Is Behind The Fresh Attention?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/software/nasdaq-evcm/evercommerce/news/evercommerce-evcm-what-is-behind-the-fresh-attention","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794544582.769,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.922,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Insider Selling: EverCommerce (NASDAQ:EVCM) Director Sells $550,001.50 in Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/insider-selling-evercommerce-nasdaqevcm-director-sells-550001-50-in-stock.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794529383.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.844,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(EVCM) Volatility Zones as Tactical Triggers","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/90/EVCM_Volatility_Zones_as_Tactical_Triggers_111126021201_1794381121.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794381121.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What EverCommerce (EVCM) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/08/what-evercommerce-evcm-said-on-its-q3-earnings-call.html","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794150916.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.402,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"EverCommerce (NASDAQ:EVCM) Issues Quarterly Earnings Results","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/08/evercommerce-nasdaqe